This is an experiment in rewriting the main website into plain HTML. No build tool.

Rationale:
* Trying things out.
* compose-html is good, but not great.
* Making interactive sections might be more complicated than plain HTML

Principles:
* TAC CSS methodology
  - default styles for semantic HTML
  - custom elements
  - attr()
  - general classes
* Offline scripts
  - RSS generator
    - microformats
* HTML first
* Interactive islands
  - Maybe not Web Components (they're currently lame)
  - No default framework, use what fits for use
    - Preact for complicated demos
    - Alpine.js (or similar) for simple interactive illustrations
    - jQuery?
    - inline adjacent <script>s
    - etc.
  - No build step (e.g. no Svelte)
